  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 10,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.046,
            0.347,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.086,
            0.848,
            0.145
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Let us consider the Carpenter’s Problem again. If the wooden strips have to be placed such that the thread passing through their endpoints forms a square, what must be done?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.157,
            0.156,
            0.393,
            0.338
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 2,
              "bbox": [
                0.157,
                0.156,
                0.393,
                0.338
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_10_image_2.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.402,
            0.148,
            0.848,
            0.203
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "As in the previous case, let us try to construct a square, one of whose diagonals is of length 8 cm."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.401,
            0.203,
            0.849,
            0.297
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "While solving the Carpenter’s Problem for the case of a rectangle, we have seen that to get a quadrilateral with all angles "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "9 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (and opposite sides of equal length), the diagonals have to be drawn such that —"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.464,
            0.3,
            0.792,
            0.322
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) they are of equal lengths, and"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.459,
            0.324,
            0.721,
            0.345
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) they bisect each other."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.35,
            0.847,
            0.41
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What more needs to be done to get equal sidelengths as well? Can this be achieved by properly choosing the angle between the diagonals? See if you can reason and/or experiment to figure this out!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.418,
            0.834,
            0.44
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Deduction 5— What should be the angle formed by the diagonals?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.449,
            0.848,
            0.505
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The angle between the diagonals can be found using the notion of congruence! Suppose we join the equal diagonals such that they bisect each other and result in a square. Let us label the square ABCD."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.504,
            0.848,
            0.542
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "To find the angle formed by the diagonals, what are the two triangles we should consider for congruence?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.547,
            0.423,
            0.74
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 11,
              "bbox": [
                0.155,
                0.547,
                0.423,
                0.74
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_10_image_11.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.423,
            0.626,
            0.846,
            0.665
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "By the SSS condition for congruence, ∆BOA ≅ ∆BOC"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.743,
            0.847,
            0.783
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Can this be used to find the angles ∠"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "BOA and",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " ∠"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "BOC",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " formed by the diagonals?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.786,
            0.848,
            0.844
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since these angles are corresponding parts of congruent triangles, they are equal. Further, these angles together form a straight angle. So "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle BOA + \\angle BOC = 180^{\\circ}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Thus, these angles have to be 90° each."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.084,
            0.915,
            0.12,
            0.936
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "92"
            }
          ]
        },
